    <name>
      <text>arithmatic-sequence-Q2</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Look at this number pattern:</p>
<p>\({@t1@}, \; {@t2@}, \; {@t3@}, \; {@t4@}, \; {@t5@}, \; \ldots\)</p>
<p>The pattern is an arithmetic progression (AP). The numbers are getting smaller.</p>

<p>(a) Find the common difference.</p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>(b) Write an expression for the \(n^{th}\) term of the pattern. Use \(n\) in your answer.</p>
<p>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>(c) Use your rule to find term number {@m@}.</p>
<p>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>

<p>(d) Which term of the pattern is equal to {@target@}?</p>
<p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3> Worked Solution.</h3>
<p>The pattern is {@t1@}, {@t2@}, {@t3@}, {@t4@}, {@t5@}, ... This is an arithmetic progression (AP). The numbers are getting smaller, so the common difference is negative.</p>

<p>(a) <strong>Common difference:</strong></p>
<p>Take the later term and subtract the earlier term:</p>
<p>\[ d = {@t2@} - {@t1@} = {@ta1@} \]</p>
<p>Check: \( {@t3@} - {@t2@} = {@ta1@} \) and \( {@t4@} - {@t3@} = {@ta1@} \). The difference is always the same. It is negative because the numbers are going down.</p>

<p>(b) <strong>The \(n^{th}\) term:</strong></p>
<p>The rule for the \(n^{th}\) term of an AP is:</p>
<p>\[ T_n = a + (n-1)d \]</p>
<p>Here the first term is \( a = {@a@} \) and the common difference is \( d = {@d@} \). Put these into the rule:</p>
<p>\[ T_n = {@a@} + (n-1) \times ({@d@}) \]</p>
<p>Open the bracket and simplify:</p>
<p>\[ T_n = {@ta2_simp@} \]</p>
<p>Check with term 1. Put \( n = 1 \) into the rule. You should get the first term, {@a@}.</p>

<p>(c) <strong>Term number {@m@}:</strong></p>
<p>Put \( n = {@m@} \) into the rule:</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@m@} } = {@a@} + ({@m@} - 1) \times ({@d@}) \]</p>
<p>\[ T_{ {@m@} } = {@a@} + {@m-1@} \times ({@d@}) = {@ta3@} \]</p>

<p>(d) <strong>Which term equals {@target@}?</strong></p>
<p>Set the rule equal to {@target@} and solve for \(n\):</p>
<p>\[ {@a@} + (n-1) \times ({@d@}) = {@target@} \]</p>
<p>Subtract {@a@} from both sides:</p>
<p>\[ (n-1) \times ({@d@}) = {@target - a@} \]</p>
<p>Divide both sides by \( ({@d@}) \):</p>
<p>\[ n - 1 = {@(target - a)/d@} \]</p>
<p>Add 1 to both sides:</p>
<p>\[ n = {@ta4@} \]</p>
<p>So {@target@} is term number {@ta4@} of the pattern.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
